Preparation of \(\mathbf{Zn}_{2}(\mathbf{DBTD})(\mathbf{DPB-CHO})\) . The \(\mathrm{Zn}_{2}(\mathrm{DBTD})(\mathrm{DPB}-\) CHO) MOF was prepared using a slightly modified literature procedure.53 In a one-dram vial, \(Z\mathrm{n}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) ( \(18.0~\mathrm{~mg~}\) , 60.5 \(\upmu\mathrm{mol})\) , \(\mathrm{H}_{4}\mathrm{DBTD}\) ( \(5.40\;\mathrm{mg}\) , \(7.50\;\upmu\mathrm{mol})\) , and DPB-CHO \((5.00\;\mathrm{mg},\,19.2\) \(\upmu\mathrm{mol})\) were dissolved in the mixture of \(0.8\mathrm{~\ensuremath~{~mL~}~}\) of \(N_{-}N\cdot\) - dimethylformamide (DMF) and \(\mathrm{HBP4}\) \((0.1\upmu\mathrm{L})\) followed by sonication. The resulting solution was placed in a preheated oven at \(80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for 24 h and then cooled down to room temperature over \(2\,\textrm{h}\) . Colorless crystals of \(Z\mathrm{n}_{2}(\mathrm{DBTD})(\mathrm{DPB-CHO})\) \((4.70~\mathrm{~mg},~4.27~\mathrm{~\upmumol})\) were isolated in \(57\%\) yield. A detailed description of the crystallographic data collection and refinement details are given in Table S1. The determined structure of \(Z\mathrm{n}_{2}(\mathrm{DBTD})(\mathrm{DPB-CHO})\) is shown in Figure S5. FTIR (neat, \(\mathrm{cm}^{-1}\) ): 2928, 1665, 1641, 1613, 1559, 1501, 1435, 1385, 1255, 1222, 1179, 1090, 1063, 1026, 1018, 905, 865, 845, 825, 787, 749, 725, and 658. The powder X-ray diffraction (PXRD) pattern of \(Z\mathrm{n}_{2}(\mathrm{DBTD})(\mathrm{DPB-CHO})\) matches the one simulated from singlecrystal \(\mathrm{X}\) -ray data (Figure S6). PXRD studies were also used to confirm crystallinity of the bulk material before and after irradiation (Figure S6). The PXRD patterns and modulation of electronic properties of \(Z\mathrm{n}_{2}(\mathrm{DBTD})(\mathrm{DPB-CHO})\) as a function of the excitation wavelength in the bulk and single-crystal forms are shown in Figures S6, S7, and S4.
